From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] diagnostics: let nested ICEs finish their diagnostic

When not checking, an ICE after an earlier error becomes a fatal error.
A deliberately nested ICE, reported within another diagnostic's group,
must still finish, so that every output sink can complete the
surrounding diagnostic; convert only top-level ones.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/gcc/diagnostics/context.cc b/gcc/diagnostics/context.cc
--- a/gcc/diagnostics/context.cc
+++ b/gcc/diagnostics/context.cc
@@ -1461,12 +1461,13 @@ context::report_diagnostic (diagnostic_info *diagnostic)
   if (diagnostic->m_kind == kind::ice || diagnostic->m_kind == kind::ice_nobt)
     {
-      /* When not checking, ICEs are converted to fatal errors when an
-	 error has already occurred.  This is counteracted by
-	 abort_on_error.  */
+      /* When not checking, top-level ICEs are converted to fatal errors when
+	 an error has already occurred.  Preserve deliberately nested ICEs so
+	 every output sink can finish the surrounding diagnostic.  */
       if (!CHECKING_P
 	  && (diagnostic_count (kind::error) > 0
 	      || diagnostic_count (kind::sorry) > 0)
-	  && !m_abort_on_error)
+	  && !m_abort_on_error
+	  && m_diagnostic_groups.m_diagnostic_nesting_level == 0)
 	{
 	  expanded_location s
 	    = expand_location (diagnostic_location (diagnostic));
